        <name>dump_lsn</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Max LSN covered by this in-memory tree. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Once the tree is dumped to disk it will be used to update <ref refid="structvy__lsm_1af88fad06d4549ced011d3f9a021be78b" kindref="member">vy_lsm::dump_lsn</ref>, see vy_task_dump_new().</para><para>Note, we account not only original LSN (vy_stmt_lsn()) in this variable, but also WAL LSN of deferred DELETE statements. This is needed to skip WAL recovery of both deferred and normal statements that have been dumped to disk. See vy_deferred_delete_on_replace() for more details. </para>        </detaileddescription>
